# The password of tally_console, the login role the console reads the engine
# database as, and the console's connection string that carries it. Copy this
# file to tally-console-db.env and generate the password with
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. db-url carries it unencoded, so `make prod-up`
# refuses a password with a character other than a letter, a digit or -._~.
#
# Job tally-migrate sets the role's password to this value on every deploy, so
# changing it and running `make prod-up` rotates the password. A rotation
# changes both values below, the password and the password inside db-url.
# TimescaleDB does not mount this Secret, so a rotation does not restart the
# database.
password=
# What the console connects to the engine database with. Put the value of
# password in place of <password>; `make prod-up` refuses a db-url that is not
# a postgres:// or postgresql:// URL as tally_console carrying it.
db-url=postgres://tally_console:<password>@timescaledb:5432/tally_engine?sslmode=disable
